1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The whole world saw — this
ladle.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Seven stars shaped like a ladle — ten
lives around the world.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Ancient Egyptians called it Meskhetyu
and drew it on coffin lids.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
From northern and eastern Europe to
China, people see a cart.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:27,000
In Homer, the Bear turns in place,
watching Orion — it alone never bathes
in the ocean.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
India: seven sages. Mongolia: seven old
men. Blackfoot: seven brothers and their
little sister.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,000
In Arabia, the bowl is a bier; the
handle, the daughters who carry it.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
In Macedonian folklore, a gang circles
all night — like thieves around a house.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:57,000
To the Amazon’s Tukano, when it touches
the horizon at dusk each year, it
swallows nearly all the river’s fish.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
For the Bugis, a ship. For Mandar
fishermen, a fishing net.

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
For the Evenki of Siberia, the bowl is a
moose’s legs; the handle, its hunter.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
It is already high. Around 23:00 it
stands highest in the north, upside
down.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Beside Mizar, faint al-Suhā was said to
test eyesight. Can you see it?

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Follow the handle’s arc to a star.

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

